{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Which have legs.</b> It is not written לו; it is read לו (i.e., written defectively without vav)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The point is that the word אשר לו is spelled without a vav in the consonantal text (לו read as if written with vav, i.e., the standard form), meaning the ketiv here is the same as the qeri; Chizkuni notes the plene/defective spelling distinction."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:18.471572829Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}